# Appendix A — Assignment Grading Rubrics
AI-Enabled Informatics for Engineers (Spring 2026)

This appendix defines grading criteria for all graded assignments (A1–A5).
Rubrics emphasize decision quality, informatics reasoning, and reproducibility.

---

## A1 — SQL + Decision Questions (Week 2)

**Purpose:** Translate decisions into data questions and answer them with SQL.

### What to Submit
- PDF or DOCX with:
  - 5 decision questions
  - 5 SQL queries
  - Output tables or screenshots
  - 1–3 sentence interpretation per query
- OR Colab notebook link with outputs visible

### Grading (100 pts)

| Category | Points | Expectations |
|--------|------|-------------|
| Decision framing | 30 | Questions specify *who decides* and *what action changes* |
| SQL correctness | 30 | Queries run; correct joins/filters/aggregations |
| Interpretation | 25 | Explicit link from output → decision |
| Clarity | 15 | Clean formatting, labels, readable structure |

### Credible Help Resources
- SQLZoo: https://sqlzoo.net/
- Kaggle Intro to SQL: https://www.kaggle.com/learn/intro-to-sql
- Kaggle datasets: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets

